dom_easy = [
    ("What are 'Domain-Specific Competencies' in workforce and administrative development?", "Specialized, in-depth technical knowledge and practical expertise unique to a specific industry, sector, or professional discipline", ["Universal interpersonal traits like empathy and polite manners", "The basic ability to read and write in one's native language", "Standard physical fitness exercises required for all citizens"], "Domain competencies represent deep sectoral subject matter expertise (e.g., agricultural agronomy, epidemiological surveillance, urban zoning)."),
    ("In the Mission Karmayogi competency architecture, how do Domain competencies differ from Functional competencies?", "Domain competencies cover sector-specific technical knowledge (e.g., power grid codes); Functional cover operational practices (e.g., budgeting)", ["Domain competencies are for private workers; Functional are for civil servants", "Domain competencies are only tested online; Functional are tested on paper", "Domain competencies apply to sports; Functional apply to academics"], "Functional competencies are cross-cutting management methods; Domain competencies are deep vertical sector-specific knowledge areas."),
    ("In agriculture domain expertise, what does 'MSP' stand for in Indian agricultural economics?", "Minimum Support Price", ["Maximum Sales Promotion", "Monitored Sowing Protocol", "Mandated Seed Price"], "MSP is a market intervention by the Government of India to insure agricultural producers against sharp drops in farm prices."),
    ("In agricultural domain management, what is an 'FPO'?", "Farmer Producer Organization (a collective legal entity owned by primary producers to achieve economies of scale)", ["Fertilizer Production Office", "Farm Pest Observation", "Field Protection Order"], "FPOs empower small and marginal farmers with aggregated bargaining power, lower input costs, and direct market access."),
    ("In public health domain competencies, what does 'Epidemiology' study?", "The distribution, determinants, patterns, and control of health and disease conditions in defined human populations", ["The surgical replacement of human heart valves", "The commercial manufacturing of private vitamins", "The legal licensing of hospital building architecture"], "Epidemiological domain expertise is essential for tracking disease outbreaks, calculating infection rates, and designing vaccination policies."),
    ("In public health, what is the primary purpose of an 'Immunization Cold Chain'?", "A temperature-controlled supply chain ensuring vaccines are kept continuously within required temperature ranges from factory to arm", ["An ice cream delivery refrigeration truck network", "A cryotherapy treatment used for sports muscle injuries", "A refrigerated morgue facility inside district hospitals"], "Maintaining temperatures (typically +2°C to +8°C) preserves vaccine potency; cold chain failures destroy immunogenicity."),
    ("In urban planning and municipal domain management, what does 'Master Plan' mean?", "A statutory comprehensive long-term blueprint guiding the physical spatial development, land use zoning, and infrastructure of a city", ["A daily schedule of street sweeping truck routes", "A financial list of municipal employee salary grades", "A collection of architectural paintings of historical monuments"], "Master plans designate residential, commercial, industrial, and green zones to ensure structured, sustainable urban growth."),
    ("In urban infrastructure, what does 'TOD' stand for in modern transport planning?", "Transit-Oriented Development", ["Traffic Operations Division", "Terminal Optimization Design", "Total Overhead Deduction"], "TOD concentrates mixed-use residential and commercial development within walking distance of high-capacity public transit nodes."),
    ("In urban sanitation, what is 'STP' in wastewater management?", "Sewage Treatment Plant", ["Solid Trash Processor", "Sanitary Tube Pipeline", "Standard Tar Pavement"], "STPs treat municipal domestic sewage using biological and chemical processes before discharging safe treated effluent into water bodies."),
    ("In the power and energy sector, what is the primary function of a 'Smart Meter'?", "An electronic device that records electricity consumption in real time and communicates data bidirectionally between consumer and utility", ["A handheld meter used to measure wind speed on hilltops", "A mechanical thermometer tracking transformer engine heat", "A device that cuts electricity whenever room temperatures drop"], "Smart meters enable automated billing, eliminate manual meter reading errors, detect power theft, and facilitate dynamic time-of-day tariffs."),
    ("In renewable energy domain expertise, what unit measures the peak electrical power capacity of a solar photovoltaic power plant?", "Megawatt-peak (MWp) or Gigawatt (GW)", ["Kilowatt-hour per liter", "Megapascal pressure", "Coulombs per cubic meter"], "MWp indicates the maximum nominal DC power output achieved by a solar PV installation under Standard Test Conditions (STC)."),
    ("In the banking and financial services (BFSI) domain, what is 'AML' compliance?", "Anti-Money Laundering (regulations and controls designed to prevent criminals from disguising illegally obtained funds as legitimate income)", ["Asset Management Ledger", "Annual Mortgage License", "Authorized Market Lender"], "AML frameworks require rigorous Customer Due Diligence (CDD), transaction monitoring, and reporting of suspicious activity reports (STR)."),
    ("In banking domain regulation, what does 'KYC' stand for?", "Know Your Customer", ["Knowledge Yield Calculation", "Key Yield Curve", "Kernel Yield Criterion"], "KYC mandates financial institutions to verify the identity and address of customers to prevent identity fraud, money laundering, and terror financing."),
    ("In banking domain regulation, what are the 'Basel Accords' (Basel I, II, III)?", "International regulatory standards issued by the Basel Committee on Banking Supervision regarding bank capital adequacy, stress testing, and market liquidity risk", ["A series of treaties on European military defense cooperation", "An environmental agreement regulating industrial chemical emissions", "A maritime law governing commercial passenger cruise ships"], "Basel III enforces minimum Tier-1 capital ratios, capital conservation buffers, and Liquidity Coverage Ratios (LCR) to ensure bank solvency."),
    ("In the education domain, what is the core structural school education reform introduced by India's National Education Policy (NEP) 2020?", "Replacing the 10+2 system with a new 5+3+3+4 pedagogical and curricular structure", ["Replacing all school teachers with automated artificial intelligence bots", "Abolishing all high school science and mathematics examinations", "Shortening school education to a total of 8 years"], "The 5+3+3+4 model spans Foundational (5 yrs), Preparatory (3 yrs), Middle (3 yrs), and Secondary (4 yrs) stages."),
    ("In education pedagogy, what is the primary focus of the 'Foundational Stage' (ages 3 to 8) under NEP 2020?", "Play-based, inquiry-based, and activity-based learning, emphasizing Foundational Literacy and Numeracy (FLN)", ["Rigid rote memorization of complex classical history textbooks", "Teaching advanced quantum computer coding languages", "Conducting high-stakes competitive entrance examinations"], "FLN ensures every child achieves foundational reading, writing, and basic arithmetic skills by Grade 3 through the NIPUN Bharat mission."),
    ("In education domain assessment, what is 'Formative Assessment'?", "Ongoing, continuous assessments conducted during the learning process to provide immediate feedback and adjust instruction", ["The final high-stakes three-hour board examination at year end", "A standardized IQ test administered for university admissions", "An evaluation of the physical cleanliness of school classrooms"], "Formative assessment (e.g., quizzes, observations, peer discussions) diagnoses learning gaps in real time to guide pedagogy."),
    ("In education assessment, what is 'Summative Assessment'?", "An evaluation administered at the conclusion of an instructional unit or year to measure cumulative learning against established standards", ["A daily ungraded five-minute homework reading assignment", "An informal conversation with a student during lunch recess", "A medical health checkup conducted by school nurses"], "Summative assessment (e.g., final term exams, board certifications) evaluates overall attainment for grading and accountability."),
    ("In environmental domain governance, what does 'EIA' stand for?", "Environmental Impact Assessment", ["Ecological Inspection Audit", "Environmental Information Agency", "Emergency Industry Authorization"], "EIA is a statutory regulatory process evaluating the potential environmental consequences of proposed infrastructure and industrial projects."),
    ("In environmental domain governance, what is the primary role of the 'State Pollution Control Board' (SPCB)?", "Enforcing environmental pollution control laws, monitoring air and water quality, and issuing regulatory Consents to Establish and Operate (CTE/CTO)", ["Inspecting the mechanical integrity of state police patrol cars", "Collecting personal income tax returns from factory employees", "Managing commercial wildlife tourism resorts inside sanctuaries"], "SPCBs enforce the Water Act 1974 and Air Act 1981, inspecting industrial discharges and prosecuting environmental violators."),
    ("In transportation domain engineering, what does 'ITS' stand for in smart highway operations?", "Intelligent Transportation Systems", ["Integrated Track Standard", "Interstate Toll System", "Internal Transit Structure"], "ITS deploys CCTV surveillance, automatic incident detection, dynamic variable message signs (VMS), and centralized traffic management."),
    ("In defense domain procurement, what does 'DAP' stand for in Indian defense modernization?", "Defense Acquisition Procedure", ["Department of Armed Police", "Direct Armament Purchasing", "Division of Artillery Production"], "DAP (formerly DPP) governs capital acquisitions for the Indian Armed Forces, prioritizing domestic indigenization (Make in India)."),
    ("In defense domain technology, what does 'iDEX' stand for?", "Innovations for Defence Excellence", ["Indian Defence Export Exchange", "Integrated Defence Explosives", "International Drone Exploration"], "iDEX engages MSMEs, startups, and individual innovators to develop cutting-edge indigenous defense and aerospace technologies."),
    ("In telecom and wireless domain engineering, what does '5G NR' stand for?", "5G New Radio (the global standard for unified 5G wireless air interface)", ["5th Generation Network Router", "General Network Relay", "Global Network Register"], "5G NR delivers ultra-high peak data rates, ultra-low latency (URLLC), and massive machine-type communications (mMTC)."),
    ("In electrical engineering domain expertise, what is the role of a 'Substation' in power transmission?", "Transforming voltage levels between high-voltage transmission and low-voltage distribution, and routing electrical power safely", ["Generating electricity from raw natural gas fuels", "Manufacturing copper electrical household cables", "Storing electricity inside chemical lithium batteries"], "Substations use step-up/step-down transformers, switchgear, and circuit breakers to regulate electrical grid stability."),
    ("In water resources domain management, what is 'Rainwater Harvesting'?", "The collection, conveyance, and storage of rainfall runoff for productive reuse or groundwater aquifer recharge", ["Seeding clouds with silver iodide chemicals to create rain", "Purifying seawater using high-pressure reverse osmosis membranes", "Bottling natural mineral spring water in commercial factories"], "Rainwater harvesting recharges depleted groundwater tables, reduces urban storm flooding, and enhances water self-sufficiency."),
    ("In forestry and ecology domain management, what is a 'Biosphere Reserve'?", "A designated protected area promoting conservation of biodiversity, sustainable economic development, and ecological research", ["A commercial timber logging concession granted to private companies", "A luxury zoo where wild animals are exhibited in cages", "A botanical greenhouse built inside a university campus"], "UNESCO Biosphere Reserves are zoned into Core (strictly protected), Buffer, and Transition zones for sustainable human coexistence."),
    ("In housing and construction domain standards, what does 'NBC' stand for in India?", "National Building Code of India", ["National Brick Classification", "Network Building Construction", "Neighborhood Building Council"], "Published by BIS, the NBC provides comprehensive safety regulations governing structural design, fire protection, and plumbing."),
    ("In civil engineering domain management, what is 'BIM'?", "Building Information Modeling (a 3D digital representation of physical and functional characteristics of a facility)", ["Basic Infrastructure Map", "Brick Installation Method", "Building Inspection Matrix"], "BIM integrates architectural, structural, and MEP data, enabling clash detection, quantity take-offs, and lifecycle maintenance."),
    ("In food safety domain regulation, what does 'FSSAI' stand for in India?", "Food Safety and Standards Authority of India", ["Federal Sanitation and Security Agency of India", "Farm Soil Science Association of India", "Food Supply and Storage Administration of India"], "FSSAI establishes science-based standards for food manufacturing, storage, distribution, and import to ensure wholesome human food."),
    ("In maritime domain governance, what does 'UNCLOS' stand for?", "United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea", ["Universal Network of Coastal Logistics and Oceanic Shipping", "Union of National Coastguards and Oceanic Sovereignty", "United Navigation Commission on Long-distance Ocean Shipping"], "UNCLOS establishes comprehensive legal frameworks governing maritime zones, territorial seas, Exclusive Economic Zones (EEZ), and seabed mining."),
    ("Under UNCLOS, what is the standard breadth of a coastal state's 'Exclusive Economic Zone' (EEZ)?", "Up to 200 nautical miles from the coastal baseline", ["Up to 12 nautical miles", "Up to 50 nautical miles", "Up to 500 nautical miles"], "The coastal state holds sovereign sovereign rights over natural resources (fisheries, petroleum, minerals) within its 200 nautical mile EEZ."),
    ("In disaster management domain operations, what are the four stages of the 'Disaster Management Cycle'?", "Mitigation, Preparedness, Response, and Recovery", ["Warning, Evacuation, Rebuilding, and Auditing", "Rescue, Shelter, Food, and Medical", "Inception, Planning, Execution, and Close"], "The DM cycle shifts focus from reactive post-disaster relief to proactive disaster risk reduction (DRR) and resilient recovery."),
    ("In Indian disaster governance, what is the statutory role of the 'NDRF'?", "National Disaster Response Force (a specialized federal paramilitary force trained for multi-hazard disaster rescue operations)", ["National Defence Reserve Fleet", "National Division of Rural Farming", "Network of District Relief Foundations"], "Constituted under the Disaster Management Act, 2005, the NDRF delivers rapid humanitarian search, rescue, and medical aid during catastrophes.")
]

dom_med = [
    ("In agriculture domain expertise, what is 'Precision Agriculture'?", "An agricultural management strategy using GPS, IoT sensors, satellite imagery, and AI to optimize field-level inputs (water, fertilizer, seeds)", ["Plowing farm fields using manual hand bullock carts", "Planting the identical crop across an entire national state", "Spraying uniform high chemical doses over all farm acreage"], "Precision farming reduces input costs and chemical runoff by tailoring irrigation and nutrients to micro-variations across soil zones."),
    ("In agricultural soil science, what does 'Soil Cation Exchange Capacity' (CEC) measure?", "The total capacity of a soil to hold, retain, and exchange positively charged nutrient ions (e.g., Ca2+, Mg2+, K+, NH4+)", ["The rate at which water evaporates from surface soil", "The total mass of earthworms living inside one acre of soil", "The mechanical hardness of dry agricultural clay"], "High CEC soils (e.g., humus and clay soils) hold abundant nutrients against leaching, releasing them steadily to plant roots."),
    ("In public health domain analytics, what is the 'Basic Reproduction Number' (R0) of an infectious disease?", "The expected average number of secondary infections generated by a single infected individual in a completely susceptible population", ["The percentage of infected patients who die from the disease", "The number of days required to manufacture a vaccine in laboratories", "The total financial expenditure incurred on quarantine hospital beds"], "If R0 > 1, the disease spreads exponentially into an epidemic; if R0 < 1, the transmission chain gradually dies out."),
    ("In epidemiology, what is 'Case Fatality Rate' (CFR) versus 'Infection Fatality Rate' (IFR)?", "CFR is deaths divided by confirmed diagnosed cases; IFR is deaths divided by total estimated infections (including asymptomatic cases)", ["CFR is for hospital patients; IFR is for animals", "CFR is calculated before an outbreak; IFR after an outbreak", "There is zero difference; both terms are identical"], "IFR reflects true biological lethality across all infected individuals, and is typically lower than CFR because many mild cases go unrecorded."),
    ("In urban planning, what is 'Floor Space Index' (FSI) or 'Floor Area Ratio' (FAR)?", "The ratio of the total covered built-up floor area of a building to the total area of the plot on which it stands", ["The physical height of a building measured in feet", "The percentage of plot area covered by green grass lawns", "The number of parking slots provided in the basement"], "FSI governs urban density: if a 1,000 sq m plot has an FSI of 2.0, total allowable built-up construction across all floors is 2,000 sq m."),
    ("In environmental engineering, what does 'BOD' (Biochemical Oxygen Demand) measure in water quality testing?", "The amount of dissolved oxygen required by aerobic microorganisms to biologically decompose organic matter in a water sample", ["The total weight of plastic garbage floating on river surfaces", "The chemical acidity measured on a standard pH sensor", "The temperature difference between river surface and bottom"], "High BOD indicates severe organic sewage pollution, depleting dissolved oxygen and killing aquatic fish populations."),
    ("In water testing, what is 'COD' (Chemical Oxygen Demand) and how does it compare to BOD?", "COD measures total oxygen required to chemically oxidize both biodegradable and non-biodegradable organic pollutants; COD is always higher than BOD", ["COD measures only drinking water mineral salts", "COD is always lower than BOD because chemicals are weak", "COD measures bacterial pathogens using microscopes"], "COD provides a rapid measure (completed in hours, whereas standard BOD takes 5 days) of total chemical industrial organic pollution."),
    ("In the electrical power grid, what does 'Grid Frequency' stability reflect in India (standard 50.00 Hz)?", "The real-time dynamic balance between total active electrical generation and total consumer power demand across the synchronous grid", ["The speed at which coal trains travel to thermal power plants", "The percentage of electricity generated from nuclear power stations", "The voltage reading of household electrical wall sockets"], "If demand exceeds generation, frequency drops below 50 Hz; if generation exceeds demand, frequency rises, risking catastrophic blackouts."),
    ("In power transmission, what is 'Ancillary Services' in grid operations?", "Operational support services (frequency regulation, spinning reserves, reactive power voltage support) contracted by the grid operator to maintain stability", ["Cleaning dust off solar photovoltaic glass panels", "Writing monthly electricity bills for residential customers", "Trimming tree branches growing near wooden power poles"], "Ancillary services ensure the grid remains resilient and stable amid intermittency from renewable wind and solar generation."),
    ("In renewable energy integration, what is the 'Duck Curve' phenomenon in solar-rich power grids?", "A daily net load curve showing a deep mid-day belly (due to abundant solar power) followed by a steep evening ramp when the sun sets", ["A curve plotting the migratory flight paths of wild ducks over wind turbines", "A chart tracking the retail market price of roasted poultry meat", "A graph showing seasonal river water discharges through hydro dams"], "The duck curve poses acute challenges: grid operators must rapidly ramp up flexible conventional or battery capacity as solar drops at twilight."),
    ("In banking domain analytics, what is the 'Net Non-Performing Asset' (NNPA) ratio?", "NNPA = (Gross NPAs - Provisions) / (Gross Advances - Provisions)", ["NNPA = Total Bank Deposits / Total Loans Given", "NNPA = Total Cash in Vaults / Total Balance Sheet Assets", "NNPA = Total Executive Salaries / Annual Net Profit"], "NNPA reflects the true bad debt risk exposure remaining on a bank's balance sheet after subtracting financial loss provisions."),
    ("In banking domain regulation, what is the 'Liquidity Coverage Ratio' (LCR) under Basel III?", "The requirement that banks hold sufficient High-Quality Liquid Assets (HQLA) to survive a severe 30-day liquidity stress scenario", ["The ratio of long-term mortgages to equity share capital", "The percentage of bank branches equipped with automated cash ATMs", "The annual dividend percentage paid out to corporate shareholders"], "LCR guarantees that a bank holds unencumbered cash and sovereign bonds to absorb sudden wholesale depositor runs for a month."),
    ("In the insurance domain, what does 'Incurred Claims Ratio' (ICR) evaluate for an insurance company?", "The total value of claims paid and provisions created divided by the total net earned premium collected (Claims / Premium * 100)", ["The percentage of insurance policy applications rejected due to illness", "The average annual bonus paid to licensed insurance sales agents", "The market valuation of the insurance company on the stock exchange"], "An ICR of ~70-80% indicates sound underwriting profitability; an ICR over 100% means claims exceed premium revenues, causing underwriting losses."),
    ("In education domain assessment under NEP 2020, what is 'PARAKH'?", "Performance Assessment, Review, and Analysis of Knowledge for Holistic Development (national assessment center setting standard evaluation norms)", ["A digital tablet given to high school physics students", "A national athletic sports championship held for universities", "A scholarship scheme funding overseas foreign education"], "PARAKH operates under NCERT, setting standardized psychometric norms, national achievement surveys (NAS), and holistic report cards."),
    ("In education pedagogy, what is the 'Competency-Based Education' (CBE) paradigm shift?", "Moving from rote memorization and rigid syllabus completion to demonstrating mastery of observable, real-world competencies and learning outcomes", ["Grading students exclusively on the number of pages they write in exams", "Forcing all students to study only mechanical vocational trades", "Conducting oral examination debates without any written textbooks"], "CBE emphasizes deep comprehension, critical application, problem-solving, and individualized learning pace over passive seat-time."),
    ("In environmental regulation, what is the 'Air Quality Index' (AQI) and how is it determined?", "A composite index converting concentrations of 8 key ambient air pollutants (PM10, PM2.5, NO2, SO2, CO, O3, NH3, Pb) into a single numeric score", ["A measure of ambient outdoor air temperature and humidity", "The percentage of oxygen present in local city atmosphere", "The wind direction recorded by airport weather radars"], "AQI simplifies complex chemical telemetry into color-coded categories (Good, Moderate, Poor, Severe) to communicate health hazards."),
    ("In environmental domain law, what does 'CRZ' (Coastal Regulation Zone) notification regulate?", "Development activities, construction, and industries within 500 meters of the High Tide Line (HTL) along coastal shorelines and tidally influenced water bodies", ["Deep-sea commercial international petroleum tanker routes", "The extraction of freshwater from inland mountain glaciers", "The commercial breeding of livestock cattle on rural plains"], "CRZ notifications protect fragile coastal ecosystems (mangroves, coral reefs) while balancing livelihoods of traditional fishing communities."),
    ("In defense domain strategy, what is 'Network-Centric Warfare' (NCW)?", "Translating an information advantage into competitive warfighting power by robustly networking sensors, command decision-makers, and shooters", ["Engaging in cyber warfare to hack commercial retail bank websites", "Using public social media websites to recruit military infantry soldiers", "Laying physical copper telephone wires between military barracks"], "NCW improves situational awareness, accelerates decision cycles (OODA loop), and enables rapid, synchronized precision kinetic strikes."),
    ("In defense domain logistics, what does 'Indigenization' target under positive indigenization lists?", "Banning the import of designated defense weapon systems, platforms, and sub-systems to compel indigenous design and manufacturing in India", ["Exporting all domestic military hardware to foreign armed forces", "Recruiting only native soldiers born in border districts", "Scrapping all existing armored tanks and artillery guns"], "MoD's positive indigenization lists stimulate private defense manufacturing clusters and enhance sovereign technological autonomy."),
    ("In healthcare domain quality, what is 'NABH' accreditation in India?", "National Accreditation Board for Hospitals & Healthcare Providers (standard for patient safety, clinical quality, and hospital governance)", ["National Association of Blood Donors and Hospital Workers", "Network of Ayurvedic Biomedicine and Herbal Clinics", "National Agency for Biological Hazards and Viral Disease"], "NABH standards benchmark clinical protocols, infection control, medication safety, and patient rights across Indian hospitals."),
    ("In telecom engineering, what is 'Spectrum Refarming'?", "Reallocating legacy frequency bands (e.g., 900 MHz or 1800 MHz formerly used for 2G/3G) to modern high-efficiency 4G/5G mobile broadband", ["Selling damaged telecommunication cellular tower metal scrap", "Digging up underground optical fiber broadband cables for cleaning", "Using radio broadcasting antennas to dry agricultural grains"], "Spectrum refarming extracts maximum spectral efficiency from prime sub-GHz coverage spectrum without requiring new frequency allocations."),
    ("In transportation infrastructure, what is 'Ballastless Track' (Slab Track) in modern high-speed rail systems?", "Railway tracks laid on reinforced concrete slabs rather than traditional crushed stone ballast gravel beds", ["Rail lines constructed without any steel metal rails", "Tracks built on floating inflatable pontoons over water rivers", "Underground railway tunnels built without concrete tunnel walls"], "Slab tracks provide superior geometric stability at high speeds (>250 km/h), eliminate flying ballast hazards, and drastically reduce maintenance."),
    ("In civil structural engineering, what does 'Pre-stressed Concrete' (PSC) achieve over standard reinforced concrete?", "Engineers apply compressive stresses using high-strength steel tendons before loading, counteracting tensile stresses under service loads", ["Concrete poured without adding any water or moisture during mixing", "Using painted plastic fibers instead of steel reinforcement bars", "Pre-heating wet concrete blocks inside industrial ovens"], "PSC enables longer bridge spans, thinner structural decks, and crack-free longevity under heavy dynamic vehicular loads."),
    ("In mining and geology domain management, what is 'Overburden' (OB)?", "The layer of soil, rock, and vegetation that lies above an underground mineral or coal seam that must be removed in open-cast mining", ["The excessive weight of mineral ore loaded onto a transport truck", "The financial debt owed by a commercial mining corporation to banks", "The psychological stress experienced by deep underground miners"], "The Stripping Ratio (volume of OB removed per ton of coal mined) dictates the economic viability of surface opencast mining."),
    ("In climate change domain science, what does 'Global Warming Potential' (GWP) measure?", "How much energy the emissions of 1 ton of a specific greenhouse gas will absorb over a given period (e.g., 100 years), relative to 1 ton of CO2", ["The maximum summer temperature recorded on global deserts", "The melting speed of polar ice caps measured in meters per year", "The total electricity generated by global solar photovoltaic panels"], "GWP allows comparison of different gases: Methane (CH4) has a GWP of ~28 over 100 years; Sulfur Hexafluoride (SF6) exceeds 23,000."),
    ("In international carbon markets, what is 'Article 6' of the Paris Agreement governing?", "Market and non-market mechanisms for international cooperation, carbon emissions trading, and Internationally Transferred Mitigation Outcomes (ITMOs)", ["The immediate dissolution of all international coal mining industries", "The deployment of military forces to enforce forest protections", "The calculation of sovereign debt write-offs for poor nations"], "Article 6.2 and 6.4 establish rigorous accounting rules to prevent double-counting of carbon credits transferred between nations."),
    ("In forest management domain governance, what is 'CAMPA' in India?", "Compensatory Afforestation Fund Management and Planning Authority (managing funds collected for diversion of forest land to non-forest purposes)", ["Central Agency for Mountain Protection and Agriculture", "Committee for Animal Management and Preservation in Asia", "Commercial Agro-forestry Marketing Promotion Authority"], "CAMPA funds collected under the Forest Conservation Act are deployed to afforest non-forest land and regenerate degraded forest tracts."),
    ("In food grain supply chain logistics, what is 'Silo' storage versus traditional 'Cover and Plinth' (CAP) storage?", "Silos are mechanized, temperature-controlled, hermetic vertical metal cylinders; CAP stores bagged grains on plinths covered by plastic tarpaulins", ["Silos are underground caves dug into mountain hills", "CAP uses automated air-conditioned concrete warehouses", "Silos store liquid chemicals; CAP stores solid coal"], "Modern steel silos eliminate rodent infestations, prevent fungal moisture spoilage, and automate bulk grain loading into railway wagons."),
    ("In public health sanitation, what does 'Faecal Sludge Management' (FSM) entail in non-sewered urban areas?", "The safe emptying, transport, treatment, and resource recovery (co-composting, biochar) of human excreta from on-site septic tanks and pit latrines", ["Dumping raw septic waste directly into municipal storm drains", "Using untreated human waste as drinking water for farm livestock", "Paving asphalt over full septic tanks without ever emptying them"], "FSM is critical for achieving ODF Plus Plus status, preventing raw pathogen discharge into urban groundwater and water bodies."),
    ("In electrical domain engineering, what is 'Power Factor' and why do industrial utilities penalize low power factor?", "The ratio of Real Power (kW) to Apparent Power (kVA); a low power factor draws excessive reactive current, causing line losses and grid strain", ["The ratio of solar energy to thermal coal generation", "The price charged per kilowatt-hour of electric power", "The mechanical horsepower generated by electric vehicle motors"], "Utilities mandate power factors near unity (0.95 to 1.0), requiring industries to install capacitor banks to correct lagging inductive loads."),
    ("In railway signaling domain engineering, what does 'ETCS' stand for in train collision protection?", "European Train Control System (an automatic train protection standard ensuring trains do not exceed authorized speeds or pass red signals)", ["Electronic Ticket Collection Service", "Emergency Track Crossing Standard", "Engine Temperature Control Sensor"], "ETCS uses trackside balises and GSM-R/LTE wireless communication to continuously supervise train movements and apply emergency brakes automatically."),
    ("What is 'KAVACH' in Indian Railways signaling and safety domain technology?", "An indigenous Automatic Train Protection (ATP) system designed to prevent train collisions (SPAD, head-on, rear-end) and enforce speed limits", ["A bulletproof metal armor installed around locomotive engines", "An electronic mobile ticketing application for passenger booking", "A track cleaning machine that removes trash from railway lines"], "KAVACH continuously transmits safety movement authorities via UHF radio, automatically applying locomotive brakes if the driver fails to act."),
    ("In electric vehicle (EV) charging domain infrastructure, what does 'CCS' stand for in DC fast charging?", "Combined Charging System (a standard connector combining AC charging pins with two high-power DC pins)", ["Centralized Current Switchboard", "Controlled Continuous Supercharger", "Core Charging Substation"], "CCS (Combo 1 and Combo 2) allows an EV to use a single inlet for both slow AC home charging and high-power DC highway fast charging.")
]

dom_hard = [
    ("In agricultural economics, how is the 'Comprehensive Cost of Cultivation' (C2 Cost) calculated for MSP determination by CACP?", "C2 = Paid-out costs (A2) + Imputed value of family labor (FL) + Rent on owned land + Interest on owned fixed capital assets", ["C2 = Only the purchase price of chemical fertilizers and seeds", "C2 = Total market retail price of food grains sold in urban supermarkets", "C2 = Transportation freight charges from farm to port"], "CACP evaluates A2 (paid expenses), A2+FL (plus family labor), and C2 (comprehensive cost); farmers demand MSP at C2 + 50%."),
    ("In infectious disease dynamic modeling, what is the 'Herd Immunity Threshold' (HIT) formula based on basic reproduction number (R0)?", "HIT = 1 - (1 / R0)", ["HIT = R0 / (1 + R0)", "HIT = (R0 - 1) * 100", "HIT = 1 / (R0^2)"], "If a disease has R0 = 4, HIT = 1 - 1/4 = 0.75 (75% of the population must be immune through vaccination or prior infection to halt transmission)."),
    ("In public health genomics, what does 'Next-Generation Sequencing' (NGS) provide in pathogen genomic surveillance?", "High-throughput, parallel sequencing of viral/bacterial genomes to rapidly detect mutations, genetic lineages, and emerging variants", ["Microscopic visual imaging of physical bacteria shapes", "Testing blood samples using chemical paper dipsticks", "Culturing living bacteria in agar petri dishes for three weeks"], "NGS (e.g., INSACOG consortium) tracked SARS-CoV-2 spike mutations in real time, detecting variants of concern before clinical surges."),
    ("In urban planning, what is 'Transferable Development Rights' (TDR) mechanism?", "A market instrument granting landowners extra floor area (FSI) certificates when their land is surrendered for public infrastructure (roads, parks)", ["The legal transfer of municipal police powers to private developers", "The right to construct skyscrapers inside national forest sanctuaries", "A property tax exemption granted to foreign multinational corporations"], "TDR compensates landowners without direct municipal cash expenditure, allowing surplus development rights to be sold for use in designated receiving zones."),
    ("In water resources engineering, what does the 'Manning Formula' calculate for open channel fluid flow?", "V = (1/n) * R^(2/3) * S^(1/2) (Flow velocity based on surface roughness n, hydraulic radius R, and channel slope S)", ["V = Pressure * Density / Temperature", "V = Acceleration * Time / Distance", "V = Gravity * Depth / Width"], "Manning's equation is the fundamental hydraulic engineering formula used to design storm water drainage canals, culverts, and sewer mains."),
    ("In high-voltage electrical grid engineering, what is the 'Ferranti Effect' on long, unloaded transmission lines?", "The voltage at the receiving end of an unloaded or lightly loaded line rises above the voltage at the sending end due to line charging capacitance", ["A sudden drop in electric current due to high conductor resistance", "The catastrophic melting of overhead aluminum wires due to lightning", "The reversal of magnetic polarity in step-up power transformers"], "Under light load, line capacitance draws charging current through line inductance; compensated by installing shunt reactors at substations."),
    ("In electrical engineering, what does 'SCADA' stand for in power grid and industrial control systems?", "Supervisory Control and Data Acquisition", ["Substation Circuit And Distribution Architecture", "Systematic Control And Diagnostic Algorithm", "Synchronous Current Allocation Data Apparatus"], "SCADA systems monitor remote telemetry, log sensor measurements, and execute real-time automated switching commands across power grids."),
    ("In smart grid architectures, what is 'Synchrophasor' technology utilizing Phasor Measurement Units (PMU)?", "High-speed sensors measuring voltage and current waveforms synchronized to GPS microsecond timestamps (30 to 60 samples per second)", ["A mechanical clock installed inside local distribution transformers", "A satellite camera tracking weather cloud formations over solar farms", "A software algorithm for calculating customer monthly electric bills"], "PMUs provide real-time dynamic wide-area situational awareness, capturing sub-second grid oscillations to prevent cascading blackouts."),
    ("In power system stability, what is 'Loss of Load Probability' (LOLP) in generation capacity planning?", "The statistical probability that system electricity demand will exceed available generation capacity over a given time horizon (e.g., 1 day in 10 years)", ["The probability that a coal train will derail on the way to a power plant", "The financial probability that an electric utility will go bankrupt", "The rate at which overhead copper wires corrode due to acid rain"], "LOLP guides capital planning, establishing required reserve margins to ensure industrial grid reliability under extreme demand spikes."),
    ("In banking domain analytics, how is the 'Capital Adequacy Ratio' (CAR / CRAR) mathematically formulated?", "CRAR = (Tier 1 Capital + Tier 2 Capital) / Total Risk-Weighted Assets (RWA)", ["CRAR = Total Bank Cash / Total Customer Loans", "CRAR = Net Profit / Total Shareholder Equity", "CRAR = Total Gross Debt / Total Fixed Assets"], "RBI mandates commercial banks maintain a minimum CRAR (typically 9% plus Capital Conservation Buffer) to absorb unexpected credit shocks."),
    ("Under Basel III, what constitutes 'Common Equity Tier 1' (CET1) capital?", "Common equity share capital, share premium, and audited retained earnings/statutory reserves (highest quality loss-absorbing capital)", ["Subordinated long-term debt and perpetual debentures", "Undisclosed hidden reserves and general loan loss provisions", "Short-term commercial paper borrowings from money markets"], "CET1 represents pure equity capable of absorbing operating losses immediately on a going-concern basis without triggering bankruptcy."),
    ("In banking credit risk modeling, what does the 'Probability of Default' (PD), 'Loss Given Default' (LGD), and 'Exposure at Default' (EAD) calculate?", "Expected Loss (EL = PD * LGD * EAD)", ["Unexpected Loss (UL = PD + LGD + EAD)", "Total Bank Net Operating Margin", "The annual interest rate charged on mortgage loans"], "Expected Loss calculations under IFRS 9 / Ind AS 109 dictate forward-looking credit loss provisioning requirements for loan portfolios."),
    ("In insurance actuarial science, what does 'Morbidity Rate' evaluate compared to 'Mortality Rate'?", "Morbidity evaluates the incidence, prevalence, and duration of disease and disability; Mortality evaluates the frequency of death", ["Morbidity evaluates financial profits; Mortality evaluates legal lawsuits", "Morbidity is calculated for animals; Mortality is calculated for humans", "Morbidity is measured in years; Mortality is measured in currency"], "Morbidity tables guide the pricing and reserve calculations of critical illness, health insurance, and disability income protection policies."),
    ("In educational psychometrics under PARAKH norms, what is 'Item Response Theory' (IRT)?", "A mathematical measurement framework that models the relationship between an individual's latent ability (theta) and the probability of answering a test item correctly", ["A method for scoring multiple-choice answer sheets using carbon paper", "A database query language for retrieving student school report cards", "An algorithm that generates random examination questions from textbooks"], "IRT estimates item difficulty, discrimination, and guessing parameters, enabling computer-adaptive testing (CAT) and test equating."),
    ("In educational assessment design, what is 'Construct-Irrelevant Variance' (CIV)?", "Error variance introduced when test scores are influenced by factors unrelated to the competency being measured (e.g., complex English vocabulary on a math test)", ["The variation in student test scores caused by differences in mathematical talent", "The physical difference in paper size between examination answer books", "The difference between morning and afternoon room temperature in test halls"], "CIV corrupts validity: a student may fail a mathematics problem not because of poor numeracy, but due to incomprehensible reading text."),
    ("In defense technology, what does 'AESA' stand for in modern fighter aircraft and naval radar systems?", "Active Electronically Scanned Array (radar beam steered electronically by thousands of solid-state transmit/receive modules with zero moving parts)", ["Automated Electronic Surveillance Apparatus", "Advanced Electro-magnetic Sonar Array", "Aerial Electronic Signal Analyzer"], "AESA radars deliver instantaneous beam steering, multi-target tracking, low probability of intercept (LPI), and high resistance to jamming."),
    ("In naval military domain doctrine, what is 'SSBN' in the strategic nuclear triad?", "Sub-Surface Ballistic Nuclear (nuclear-powered submarine armed with nuclear submarine-launched ballistic missiles - SLBMs)", ["Surface Ship Battlecruiser Nuclear", "Strategic Sea Border Patrol Vessel", "Standard Submarine Battery Network"], "SSBNs (such as INS Arihant) provide an invulnerable second-strike retaliatory capability, completing India's credible minimum deterrence."),
    ("In military artillery engineering, what does 'MRSI' (Multiple Rounds Simultaneous Impact) capability mean?", "Firing multiple artillery shells at differing trajectories and propellant charges so all shells hit the target at the exact same split second", ["Firing continuous machine gun rounds for 24 hours without stopping", "Firing artillery shells simultaneously in four opposite directions", "Dropping explosive cluster bombs from high-altitude aircraft"], "MRSI saturates enemy defenses instantaneously with maximum blast shock before defensive forces can scramble into trenches."),
    ("In environmental economics, what does 'Pigouvian Tax' mean?", "A tax levied on market activities that generate negative externalities (e.g., carbon tax on fossil fuels, pollution effluent fees)", ["A corporate tax levied on agricultural organic farming cooperatives", "A luxury tax charged on foreign imported champagne wines", "A flat payroll tax deducted from all factory worker salaries"], "Pigouvian taxes internalize external environmental costs, aligning private economic incentives with broader social and ecological welfare."),
    ("In biodiversity conservation, what does the 'EDGE of Existence' programme evaluate for species prioritization?", "Evolutionarily Distinct and Globally Endangered (prioritizing unique species with few close relatives on the tree of life facing extinction)", ["Species living exclusively on the physical geographic edges of forests", "Species that possess the highest economic commercial market value", "Species that have evolved within the past five hundred years"], "EDGE metrics channel conservation resources toward genetically irreplaceable lineages (e.g., Gharial, Purple Frog) facing imminent loss."),
    ("In nuclear engineering, what is 'Fast Breeder Reactor' (FBR) in India's three-stage nuclear power programme?", "A nuclear reactor using fast neutrons to breed more fissile material (Plutonium-239 from Uranium-238) than it consumes as fuel", ["A reactor that generates electrical power at twice the speed of light", "A reactor that uses ordinary river water without any nuclear fuel rods", "A thermal coal power station converted into an atomic energy plant"], "FBRs (Stage II, e.g., PFBR at Kalpakkam) multiply nuclear fuel resources, preparing the transition to Thorium utilization (Stage III)."),
    ("In India's three-stage nuclear power programme, what is the planned fuel cycle for the ultimate Stage III?", "Thorium-232 / Uranium-233 fuel cycle in Advanced Heavy Water Reactors (AHWR) to exploit vast domestic monazite sands", ["Enriched Uranium-235 light water reactors imported from abroad", "Natural Uranium heavy water reactors using Canadian technology", "Pure Plutonium fast reactors operating without coolant"], "India holds over 25% of global Thorium reserves; Stage III achieves long-term energy independence by converting fertile Thorium into fissile U-233."),
    ("In chemical industrial safety, what is a 'BLEVE'?", "Boiling Liquid Expanding Vapor Explosion (a catastrophic failure of a pressurized vessel containing liquid above its boiling point)", ["A slow, harmless release of non-toxic nitrogen gas", "A standard chemical cleaning procedure used in oil refineries", "An electrical short-circuit occurring inside industrial motors"], "BLEVEs generate devastating blast waves, severe projectile fragmentation, and massive expanding fireballs (e.g., LPG tanker failures)."),
    ("In chemical plant process safety, what does 'HAZOP' stand for?", "Hazard and Operability Study (a structured, systematic technique using guide words to identify process deviations and safety risks)", ["Hazardous Agricultural Zone Operating Plan", "Health And Zero Occupational Pollution", "Hardware Assessment and Zone Optimization"], "HAZOP teams apply guide words (NO, MORE, LESS, AS WELL AS, REVERSE) across piping and instrumentation diagrams (P&ID) to spot latent hazards."),
    ("In transportation economics, what does 'Induced Demand' (Braess's Paradox) dictate regarding urban road expansions?", "Expanding highway road capacity often fails to reduce congestion because the new supply encourages more driving, rapidly filling new lanes", ["Building wider highways permanently eliminates traffic jams forever", "Drivers will immediately sell their personal cars if roads are paved", "Traffic congestion is caused exclusively by public bus transit routes"], "Induced demand demonstrates that supply-side highway widening without road pricing or public transit investment accelerates car dependency."),
    ("In railway signaling engineering, what is 'Axle Counter' in track clear verification?", "An electronic sensor device detecting and counting the number of train wheel axles entering and exiting a track block to prove track vacancy", ["A mechanical device counting tickets sold to passengers at stations", "A speedometer measuring the rotating speed of train wheel axles", "A sensor calculating the weight of luggage carried by travelers"], "Axle counters operate immune to flood submergence and rusted rail surfaces, replacing traditional electrical track circuits."),
    ("In aviation domain operations, what is 'ADS-B' in air traffic management?", "Automatic Dependent Surveillance-Broadcast (aircraft broadcast their satellite GPS position, altitude, and velocity periodically to ground ATC)", ["Automated Drone Surveillance Bureau", "Aerial Defense Signal Beacon", "Aviation Distance Standard Board"], "ADS-B replaces traditional rotating radar sweeps, providing high-precision real-time aircraft tracking over continental and oceanic airspace."),
    ("In petroleum geology and reservoir engineering, what is 'Enhanced Oil Recovery' (EOR)?", "Techniques (gas injection, thermal steam, chemical polymer flooding) deployed to extract crude oil unrecoverable by primary and secondary recovery", ["Refining crude oil into commercial aviation turbine fuel", "Drilling shallow surface water wells in agricultural villages", "Transporting petroleum barrels using high-speed rail tankers"], "EOR alters fluid viscosity or interfacial tension, boosting recovery factors from typical 20-40% baselines up to 60% of original oil in place."),
    ("In mining domain safety, what is 'Acid Mine Drainage' (AMD)?", "The outflow of highly acidic water containing toxic heavy metals formed when sulfide minerals (e.g., pyrite) are exposed to air and water", ["A chemical acid pumped into underground mines to dissolve gold ores", "The runoff of rainwater from factory administrative office roofs", "An industrial acid used to clean mechanical mining drill bits"], "AMD severely contaminates regional watersheds, lowering pH to toxic levels and dissolving heavy metals that poison aquatic ecosystems."),
    ("In agriculture domain biotechnology, what is 'Biofortification'?", "Breeding crops to increase their nutritional value (e.g., zinc-enriched rice, iron-rich pearl millet) through agronomy, conventional breeding, or biotechnology", ["Applying toxic chemical pesticides to preserve packaged food grains", "Spraying colored food dyes onto unripened fruit crops", "Constructing high concrete fences around agricultural farm fields"], "Biofortification provides a sustainable, rural-accessible dietary intervention to eradicate hidden hunger and micro-nutrient deficiencies."),
    ("In public health policy, what is 'One Health' approach championed by WHO, FAO, WOAH, and UNEP?", "An integrated, unifying approach recognizing that human health, animal health, and environmental ecosystem health are inextricably linked", ["A universal health insurance scheme covering only one person per family", "A policy mandating that every village have exactly one civil hospital", "A health guideline recommending people take only one pill daily"], "One Health coordinates cross-sectoral surveillance to combat zoonotic spillover (e.g., rabies, avian flu) and Antimicrobial Resistance (AMR)."),
    ("In healthcare domain quality, what is 'Antimicrobial Resistance' (AMR) and what drives its critical global surge?", "Microorganisms evolving resistance to antimicrobial drugs, accelerated by excessive, indiscriminate antibiotic misuse in humans and livestock", ["The immunity developed by human beings after drinking boiled milk", "The resistance of hospital physical walls to structural earthquake damage", "A genetic trait preventing mosquitoes from flying in cold weather"], "The WHO classifies AMR among the top 10 global public health threats; unchecked AMR could render routine surgeries and minor infections fatal."),
    ("In environmental domain governance, what is 'Extended Producer Responsibility' (EPR)?", "An environmental policy approach holding manufacturers and brand owners financially and operationally responsible for the end-of-life management of their products", ["Holding retail customers legally responsible for repairing broken goods", "A government subsidy paying for all factory electricity bills", "An annual bonus paid to companies that manufacture plastic bottles"], "EPR mandates plastic, electronic waste (e-waste), and battery manufacturers to collect and recycle prescribed percentages of post-consumer waste.")
]
